`zoxide query` prints folders only in its own ranking, which weighs how
often against how lately, so a folder visited a hundred times last month
outranks the one visited a minute ago. The launcher's Recent lists a
program's things newest first, so it asks for `--sort-by last-accessed`:
the newest visit first. It follows upstream's own proposal for the flag
(ajeetdsouza/zoxide#857, closed unreviewed; #784 asks for it), with the
path and score orders it offered beside it. It goes on after
queries-leave-the-database-alone.patch and, like the sorts there, marks
nothing changed, since every reader sorts again.

